<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>3.2.4.2 Using the Quadratic Formula</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Use the quadratic formula to solve the equation \[ {@ex@} = 0. \]</p>
<p>Give the solutions as a set, for example \(\{-3, 2/5\}\).</p>
<div>\(x \in \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>For \(ax^2 + bx + c = 0\) the <strong>quadratic formula</strong> gives \[ x = \dfrac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}. \] First identify the coefficients, taking care with their signs, then substitute.</p>
<p>Here \(a = {@aa@}\), \(b = {@bb@}\) and \(c = {@cc@}\).</p>
<p>The <strong>discriminant</strong> is \(b^2 - 4ac = ({@bb@})^2 - 4 \times {@aa@} \times ({@cc@}) = {@dd@}\), and \(\sqrt{@dd@} = {@sd@}\).</p>
\[ x = \dfrac{{@-bb@} \pm {@sd@}}{{@2*aa@}}, \]
<p>so \(x = \dfrac{{@-bb+sd@}}{{@2*aa@}} = {@(-bb+sd)/(2*aa)@}\) or \(x = \dfrac{{@-bb-sd@}}{{@2*aa@}} = {@(-bb-sd)/(2*aa)@}\).</p>
<p>The solutions are where the graph of \(y = {@ex@}\) crosses the \(x\)-axis:</p>
<div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Graph of y = {#ex#}, crossing the x-axis at x = {#pp/aa#} and x = {#r2#}.">
[[jsxgraph width="360px" height="300px"]]
(function() {
  var f = function(x){ return {#aa#}*x*x + ({#bb#})*x + ({#cc#}); };
  var xs = [{#float(pp/aa)#},{#r2#}];
  var lo = Math.min.apply(null, xs), hi = Math.max.apply(null, xs);
  var xmin = lo - 2, xmax = hi + 2, ymin = 0, ymax = 0;
  for (var t = xmin; t <= xmax; t += (xmax - xmin)/100) { var v = f(t); ymin = Math.min(ymin, v); ymax = Math.max(ymax, v); }
  var pad = (ymax - ymin)*0.12 + 1;
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[xmin, ymax + pad, xmax, ymin - pad], axis:true, grid:false,
      showNavigation:false, showCopyright:false});
  b.create('functiongraph', [f], {strokeColor:'#1f5fa8', strokeWidth:2});
  for (var i = 0; i < xs.length; i++) {
    b.create('point', [xs[i], 0], {name:'', size:4, fixed:true, color:'#c0392b'});
  }
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
